A||||10||Carrolles||Latest G-Tech Pro results on Groom's 2.8||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||08-06-2001||08:59 AM||||In early 1999 I installed a Groom's 2.8 long block in my 85SE v-6 4spd.  During the re-build I also ported the intake and exhaust manifolds and replaced several sensors.<P>So far the engine has been great.  At the time I chose the 2.8 re-man because Grooms offered an 18 month unlimited mileage warranty only on the 2.8.  Now I think they offer the same on the 3.4.  Oh well.<P>I took the car out and made several runs using the G-Tech Pro the other day.  I managed a 7.5 second 0 to 60 with a 15.2 second 90.1 mhp quarter mile.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||08-06-2001||03:42 PM||||My engine has a 3 year/75000 mi warrenty on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good times though!  I wish I could borrow a G-tech pro and test out my stock system just for the heck of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||08-06-2001||04:11 PM||||My engine has a 3 year/unlimited mile warranty.  You can also get a 3.4 with no core charge for the same price as a 2.8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
