Z||000009||Capt Fiero||08-06-2001||06:44 PM||||Admitidly I got my motor done for cheap, becuase one of my friends worked at a local parts store that was closing up shop and sold me most of parts for what they would have gotten out of them by sending em back, plus all my machine work was done by a friend that worked in an engine building shop. I paid 1800$ roughly CDN, I think that is about 1200$ US Funds for my motor. My best G-Tech runs were 0-60 in 6.2 and 1/4 mile in 14.9 at 96mph. The motor is a bored 2.8 out to 2.9 with a big cam and other mods. I did all the assembly on the long block the machine shop did the assembly on the short block. <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||08-06-2001||07:02 PM||||14.59@99 mph with stock 3.4- cast Camaro manifolds, dual exhaust, msd 6a/Blaster coil, custom intake, Crane 11mm FireWires, Ford Motorsport 24lb injectors, '749 ecm with custom chip (Thanks!!!-you know who you are). I have the rev limiter set at a low 5200 rpms and full throttle upshift when the engine stumbles. This is the best of 3 or 4 runs, worst was a 14.80. One more small bolt on should get me into the 13's. . . ||||reg||1
